# SVG Rules

## Core Principles
- SVG (Scalable Vector Graphics) is an XML-based format for vector graphics
- Vector-based graphics scale without losing resolution quality
- Can be styled with CSS and manipulated with JavaScript
- Integrates well with HTML for web applications
- Supports animation and interactivity

## Basic Structure
- SVG documents start with the `<svg>` root element
- Coordinate system starts at top-left (0,0) and extends right and down
- Width and height attributes define the viewport size
- viewBox attribute controls the coordinate system
- preserveAspectRatio determines how SVG scales

## Shape Elements
- `<rect>` - Rectangles with x, y, width, height, rx, ry attributes
- `<circle>` - Circles with cx, cy, r attributes
- `<ellipse>` - Ellipses with cx, cy, rx, ry attributes
- `<line>` - Lines with x1, y1, x2, y2 attributes
- `<polyline>` - Connected lines with points attribute
- `<polygon>` - Closed shapes with points attribute
- `<path>` - Complex shapes using the d attribute

## Path Syntax
- M/m - moveto (absolute/relative)
- L/l - lineto (absolute/relative)
- H/h - horizontal lineto (absolute/relative)
- V/v - vertical lineto (absolute/relative)
- C/c - curveto (absolute/relative)
- S/s - smooth curveto (absolute/relative)
- Q/q - quadratic Bézier curve (absolute/relative)
- T/t - smooth quadratic Bézier curve (absolute/relative)
- A/a - elliptical arc (absolute/relative)
- Z/z - closepath

## Text Elements
- `<text>` - Creates text elements
- `<tspan>` - Sub-portions of text for styling
- `<textPath>` - Text along a path
- Attributes include x, y, dx, dy, rotate, textLength, lengthAdjust

## Styling
- Presentation attributes: fill, stroke, stroke-width
- CSS styling via style attribute or external CSS
- Classes and IDs for targeting elements
- Inline styles take precedence over CSS
- inherit keyword inherits parent's value

## Transformations
- transform attribute for geometric transformations
- translate(x, y) - move elements
- rotate(angle, [x, y]) - rotate elements
- scale(x, [y]) - resize elements
- skewX(angle) and skewY(angle) - skew elements
- matrix(a, b, c, d, e, f) - custom transformation matrix

## Grouping
- `<g>` element groups related shapes
- Transformations and styles on the group affect all children
- Groups can be nested for complex structures
- `<defs>` for defining reusable elements (not rendered directly)

## Reusable Elements
- `<symbol>` - Define reusable SVG elements
- `<use>` - Reference and instantiate reusable elements
- `<marker>` - Define markers for line endpoints
- `<pattern>` - Define repeating patterns for fills
- `<clipPath>` - Define clipping regions

## Animation
- SMIL-based animations with `<animate>`, `<animateTransform>`, `<animateMotion>`
- CSS animations for simpler animations
- JavaScript animations for complex interactions
- requestAnimationFrame for smooth animations

## Filters
- `<filter>` - Container for filter effects
- Filter primitives like feGaussianBlur, feColorMatrix, feBlend
- Filter effects can be chained
- Coordinate system defined by filterUnits and primitiveUnits

## Gradients
- `<linearGradient>` - Linear color transitions
- `<radialGradient>` - Radial color transitions
- `<stop>` elements define color stops
- Attributes include gradientUnits, spreadMethod, gradientTransform

## SVG in HTML
- Inline SVG directly in HTML5 documents
- `<img>` tag to embed external SVG files
- CSS background-image for decorative SVG
- Object or iframe for interactive external SVGs

## Accessibility
- Use title and desc elements for descriptions
- Implement ARIA attributes where appropriate
- Ensure sufficient color contrast
- Provide text alternatives for complex graphics

## Performance
- Minimize path complexity and number of nodes
- Use symbols and reuse elements with `<use>`
- Apply CSS classes instead of inline styles
- Optimize with tools like SVGO
- Consider lazy loading for large or multiple SVGs

## Browser Compatibility
- Test across browsers for consistent rendering
- Consider polyfills for older browsers
- Be aware of mobile device limitations
- Use feature detection when using advanced features

## Animation Best Practices
- Prefer CSS animations for simple transitions
- Use requestAnimationFrame for JavaScript animations
- Animate transform properties for better performance
- Minimize DOM updates during animations
- Consider reduced motion preferences

## SVG Editors
- Use dedicated SVG editors for complex graphics
- Export optimized SVG from vector design tools
- Clean up unnecessary attributes and metadata
- Validate SVG markup for standards compliance
